{"act_id": "IND_state_19319", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19319_s010", "title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "chapter": "III", "section_number": "10", "section_title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "text": "Act: The Waqf Act, 1995 (Act 43 of 1995) | India | State | In Force\nChapter III: CENTRAL[1] [WAQF] COUNCIL | Section 10: Finance of Council\n\n**10. Finance of Council.—** ( _1_ ) Every Board shall pay from its[1] [Waqf] Fund annually to the Council such contribution as is equivalent to one per cent. of the aggregate of the net annual income of the 2[auqaf] in respect of which contribution is payable under sub-section ( _1_ ) of section 72:\n\nProvided that where the Board, in the case of any particular[1] [waqf] has remitted under sub-section ( _2_ ) of section 72 the whole of the contribution payable to it under sub-section ( _1_ ) of that section, then for calculating the contribution payable to the Council under this section the net annual income of the[1] [waqf] in respect of which such remission has been granted shall not be taken into account.\n\n( _2_ ) All monies received by the Council under sub-section ( _1_ ) and all other monies received by it as donations, benefactions and grants shall form a fund to be called the Central[1] [Waqf] Fund.\n\n( _3_ ) Subject to any rules that may be made by the Central Government in this behalf, the Central 1[Waqf] Fund shall be under the control of the Council and may be applied for such purposes as the Council may deem fit.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1995.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19319?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19319/act.pdf", "record_id": "c015397b65c2fb1bb1bb", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 171, "original_text_length": 1283, "cleaned_text_length": 1283, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s003_31", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "", "section_number": "3", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nSection 3(31): \"motorcab\" means any motor vehicle constructed or adapted to carry not more than six passengers excluding the driver for hire or reward ;\n\n(31) \"permit\" means a permit issued by a State or Regional Transport Authority or an authority prescribed in this behalf under this Act authorising the use of motor vehicle as a transport vehicle ;\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ - Section 2 (31) corresponds to section 2 (20) of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1939.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "discretionary", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939", "Road Transport Corporations Act, 1950"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf", "record_id": "f0288bfdaae5f62bcca7", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 172, "original_text_length": 533, "cleaned_text_length": 533, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s065_p1", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "65", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 65: Power of the State Government to make rules.** - (1) A State Government may make rules for the purpo\n\n(h) the exemption of prescribed persons or prescribed classes of persons from payment of all or any portion of the fees payable under this Chapter.\n\n(i) the forms, other than those prescribed by the Central Government to be used for the purposes of this Chapter;\n\n(j) the communication between registering authorities of particulars of certificates of registration and by owners of vehicles registered outside the State of particulars of such vehicles and of their registration;\n\n(k) the amount or amounts under sub-section (13) of section 41 or sub-section (7) of section 47 or sub-section (4) of section 49 or sub-section (5) of section 50;\n\n(l) the extension of the validity of certificate of fitness pending consideration of applications for their renewal;\n\n(m)the extension from the provisions of this Chapter, and the conditions and fees for exemption, of motor vehicles in the possession of dealers;\n\n(n) the form in which and the period within which the return under section 62 shall be sent;\n\n(o) the manner in which the State Register of Motor Vehicles shall be maintained under section 63;\n\n(p) any other matter which is to be or may be prescribed.\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ - Section 65 corresponds to section 41 of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1939.\n\n_**Objects and Reasons.**_ - Clause 65 empowers the State Government to make rules for the purpose of carrying into effect the provisions of this Chapter.\n\n## ***CHAPTER V**\n\n## **CONTROL OF TRANSPORT VEHICLES**", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf", "record_id": "eadd0804d6d49f3adc3f", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 173, "original_text_length": 1677, "cleaned_text_length": 1677, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19316", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19316_b000_4_d1", "title": "The Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act 1986", "chapter": "", "section_number": "", "section_title": "The Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act 1986", "text": "Act: The Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act 1986 (Act 61 of 1986) | India | State | In Force\n(4): Preamble\n\n(4) No child shall be permitted or required to work between 7 p.m. and 8 a.m.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['labour_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Factories Act, 1948", "Mines Act, 1952", "Merchant Shipping Act, 1958", "Motor Transport Workers Act, 1961", "Plantations Labour Act, 1951", "Children Act, 1938", "Minimum Wages Act, 1948"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1986.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19316?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19316/act.pdf", "record_id": "48ee3e5f8dd1714bb292", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 174, "original_text_length": 196, "cleaned_text_length": 196, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19319", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19319_s048_p0", "title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "48", "section_title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "text": "Act: The Waqf Act, 1995 (Act 43 of 1995) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: ## MAINTENANCE OF ACCOUNTS OF[2] [AUQAF] | Section 48: Board to pass orders on auditor's report\n\n**48. Board to pass orders on auditor's report.—** ( _1_ ) The Board shall examine the auditor's report, and may call for the explanation of any person in regard to any matter mentioned therein, and shall pass such orders as it thinks fit including orders for the recovery of the amount certified by the auditor under sub-section ( _2_ ) of section 47.\n\n( _2_ ) The mutawalli or any other person aggrieved by any order made by the Board may, within thirty days of the receipt by him of the order, apply to the Tribunal to modify or set aside the order and the Tribunal may, after taking such evidence as it may think necessary, confirm or modify the order or remit the amount so certified, either in whole or in part, and may also make such order as to costs as it may think appropriate in the circumstances of the case.\n\n( _3_ ) No application made under sub-section ( _2_ ) shall be entertained by the Tribunal unless the amount certified by the auditor under sub-section ( _2_ ) of section 47 has first been deposited in the Tribunal and the Tribunal shall not have any power to stay the operation of the order made by the Board under sub-section ( _1_ ).\n\nTribunal shall not have any power to stay the operation of the order made by the Board under\n\n( _4_ ) The order made by the Tribunal under sub-section ( _2_ ) shall be final.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1995.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19319?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19319/act.pdf", "record_id": "740c0a3e3f66dc93dda4", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 176, "original_text_length": 1511, "cleaned_text_length": 1511, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19150", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19150_s001_7", "title": "The constitution of india", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The constitution of india", "text": "Act: The constitution of india | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: .—SPECIAL DIRECTIVES | Section 1(7): to entertain and dispose of appeals and petitions from or in respect of any judgment, decree or order of any court within that State shall cease, and all appeals and other proceedings pending before the said authority at such commencement shall be transferred to, and disposed of by, the Supreme Court.\n\n(7) The High Court for the State shall not have any powers of superintendence over the Administrative Tribunal and no court (other than the Supreme Court) or tribunal shall exercise any jurisdiction, power or authority in respect of any matter subject to the jurisdiction, power or authority of, or in relation to, the Administrative Tribunal.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['constitutional_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Bombay Reorganisation Act, 1960", "Nagaland Act, 1962", "India Act, 1935", "States Reorganisation Act, 1956", "The Indian Independence Act, 1947", "Privy Council Jurisdiction Act, 1949"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": null, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19150?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19150/act.pdf", "record_id": "65bd875b6936a56a72d1", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 177, "original_text_length": 754, "cleaned_text_length": 754, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s003_35", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "", "section_number": "3", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nSection 3(35): \"motorcab\" means any motor vehicle constructed or adapted to carry not more than six passengers excluding the driver for hire or reward ;\n\n(35) \"public service vehicle\" means any motor vehicle used or adapted to be used for the carriage of passengers for hire or reward, and includes a maxicab, a motorcab, contract carriage, and stage carriage ;\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ - Section 2 (35) corresponds to section 2 (25) of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1939.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "discretionary", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939", "Road Transport Corporations Act, 1950"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf", "record_id": "2bdafcd365dbdc3652a1", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 181, "original_text_length": 543, "cleaned_text_length": 543, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19015", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19015_s001_p0", "title": "The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016", "chapter": "I", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016", "text": "Act: The rights of persons with disabilities act, 2016 (Act 49 of 2016) | India | State | In Force\nChapter I: PRELIMINARY | Section 1: 19th April, 2017, _vide_ notification no. S.O. 1215 (E) dated 19th April, 2017, _see_ Gazette of India, Extraordinary, Part II, Section 3 (ii)\n\n> 1. 19th April, 2017, _vide_ notification no. S.O. 1215 (E) dated 19th April, 2017, _see_ Gazette of India, Extraordinary, Part II, Section 3 (ii).\n\n( _d_ ) \"care-giver\" means any person including parents and other family Members who with or without payment provides care, support or assistance to a person with disability;\n\n( _e_ ) \"certifying authority\" means an authority designated under sub-section ( _1_ ) of section 57;\n\n( _f_ ) \"communication\" includes means and formats of communication, languages, display of text, Braille, tactile communication, signs, large print, accessible multimedia, written, audio, video, visual displays, sign language, plain-language, human-reader, augmentative and alternative modes and accessible information and communication technology;\n\n( _g_ ) \"competent authority\" means an authority appointed under section 49;\n\n( _h_ ) \"discrimination\" in relation to disability, means any distinction, exclusion, restriction on the basis of disability which is the purpose or effect of impairing or nullifying the recognition, enjoyment or exercise on an equal basis with others of all human rights and fundamental freedoms in the political, economic, social, cultural, civil or any other field and includes all forms of discrimination and denial of reasonable accommodation;\n\n( _i_ ) \"establishment\" includes a Government establishment and private establishment;\n\n( _j_ ) \"Fund\" means the National Fund constituted under section 86;", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Companies Act, 2013", "Cantonments Act, 2006"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 2016.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19015?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19015/act.pdf", "record_id": "b99f776f170b7014ca5a", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 184, "original_text_length": 1742, "cleaned_text_length": 1742, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19150", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19150_s001_3_d10", "title": "The constitution of india", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The constitution of india", "text": "Act: The constitution of india | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: .—SPECIAL DIRECTIVES | Section 1(3): to entertain and dispose of appeals and petitions from or in respect of any judgment, decree or order of any court within that State shall cease, and all appeals and other proceedings pending before the said authority at such commencement shall be transferred to, and disposed of by, the Supreme Court.\n\n(3) Nothing in this Constitution shall operate to invalidate the exercise of jurisdiction by His Majesty in Council to dispose of appeals and petitions from, or in respect of, any judgment, decree or order of any court within the territory of India in so far as the exercise of such jurisdiction is authorised by law, and any order of His Majesty in Council made on any such appeal or petition after the commencement of this Constitution shall for all purposes have effect as if it were an order or decree made by the Supreme Court in the exercise of the jurisdiction conferred on such Court by this Constitution.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['constitutional_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Bombay Reorganisation Act, 1960", "Nagaland Act, 1962", "India Act, 1935", "States Reorganisation Act, 1956", "The Indian Independence Act, 1947", "Privy Council Jurisdiction Act, 1949"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": null, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19150?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19150/act.pdf", "record_id": "d8a4eefc68eccb09b0ca", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 185, "original_text_length": 1024, "cleaned_text_length": 1024, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s041_14_d1", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "41", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 41(14): Registration, how to be made.** - (1) An application by or on behalf of the owner of a motor vehicle\n\n**officers, etc.** - (1) Where an application for registration of a motor vehicle is made under sub-section (1) of section 41 by or on behalf of any diplomatic officer or consular officer, then notwithstanding anything contained in sub section (3) or sub-section (6) of that section, the registering authority shall register the vehicle in such manner and in accordance with such procedure as may be provided by\n\nrules made in this behalf by the Central Government under sub-section (3) and shall assign to the vehicle for display thereon a special registration mark in accordance with the provisions contained in those rules and shall issue a certificate ( hereafter in this\n\n20. Substituted for \"original registering authority\" by Act 54 of 1994, S.14 (w.e.f. 14-11 1994).\n\nsection referred to as the certificate of registration ) that the vehicle has been registered under this section ; and any vehicle so registered shall not, so long as it remains the property of any diplomatic officer or consular officer, require to be registered otherwise under this Act.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf", "record_id": "bfdf28c49f0923f466a8", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 186, "original_text_length": 1275, "cleaned_text_length": 1275, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19025", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19025_s017_3_d1", "title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "chapter": "", "section_number": "17", "section_title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "text": "Act: The mimimum wates act, 1948 (Act 11 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nSection 17(3): Minimum time rate wages for piece work\n\n(b) examine any person whom he finds in any such premises or place and who, he has reasonable cause to believe, is an employee employed therein or an employee to whom work is given out therein;\n\n(c) require any person giving out-work and any out-workers, to give any information, which is in his power to give, with respect to the names and addresses of the persons to, for and from whom the work is given out or received, and with respect to the payments to be made for the work;\n\n1*[(d) seize or take copies of such register, record of wages or notices or portions thereof as he may consider relevant in respect of an offence under this Act which he has reason to believe has been committed by an employer; and]\n\n(e) exercise such other powers as may be prescribed. --------------------------------------------------------------------1. Subs. by Act 30 of 1957, s. 11, for the original clause. 212", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "notification", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Factories Act, 1934"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19025?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19025/act.pdf", "record_id": "46771c439e84c8b80d74", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 187, "original_text_length": 1031, "cleaned_text_length": 1031, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s009_p0", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "9", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 9: Sub-S. (2) substituted by Act 54 of 1994, S. 28 ( w.e.f. 14-11-1994 ). Prior to its substitution, sub-S. (2) read as under :-\n\n59. Sub-S. (2) substituted by Act 54 of 1994, S. 28 ( w.e.f. 14-11-1994 ). Prior to its substitution, sub-S. (2) read as under :-\n\n\"(2) The State Government shall constitute for the State, a State Transport Appellate Tribunal which shall consist of a judicial officer who is not below the rank of a District Judge, or who is qualified to be a judge of a High Court :\n\nProvided that in relation to a Union territory, the Tribunal may consist of the Administrator of that territory or any officer who has judicial experience\".\n\nappeal lies, and if it appears to the State Transport Appellate Tribunal that the order made by the State Transport Authority or Regional Transport Authority is improper or illegal, the State Transport Appellate Tribunal may pass such order in relation to the case as it deems fit and every such order shall be final :\n\nProvided that the State Transport Appellate Tribunal shall not entertain any application from a person aggrieved by an order of a State Transport Authority or Regional Transport Authority, unless the application is made within thirty days from the date of the order :\n\nProvided further that the State Transport Appellate Tribunal may entertain the application after the expiry of the said period of thirty days, if it is satisfied that the\n\napplicant was prevented by good and sufficient cause from making the application in time :", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf", "record_id": "66f28743440b9188ecd9", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 190, "original_text_length": 1608, "cleaned_text_length": 1608, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
