{"act_id": "IND_state_18999", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18999_s118_2_d1", "title": "The factories act, 1948", "chapter": "XI", "section_number": "118", "section_title": "The factories act, 1948", "text": "Act: The factories act, 1948 (Act 63 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XI: SUPPLEMENTAL\n107.\nAppeals.\n107. Appeals. (1) The manager of a factory on whom an order in\nwriting by an Inspector has been served under the provisions or this\nAct or\n---------------------------------------------------------------------\n1. Ins. by Act 94 of 1976 s. 43 (w.e.f. 26-10-1976).\n2. Ins. by Act 20 of 1987 s. 40 (w.e.f. 1-12-1987).\n3. Ins. by Factory (Jharkhand Amendment)Act,2015, Act 24 of\n2016 (No.LG-45/2015-188/LJ dt.28.11.2016)\n``` | Section 118(2): Restriction on disclosure of information. (1) No Inspector\n\n(2) No inspector shall, which making an inspection under this\nAct, disclose to the occupier, manager or his representative that the\ninspection is made in pursuance of the receipt of complaint:\nProvided that nothing in this sub-section shall apply to any case\nin which the person who has made the complaint has consented to\ndisclose his name.]\n```\n\n```", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18999?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18999/act.pdf", "record_id": "cd9e860c46e6bee8a667", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number