{"act_id": "IND_state_19010", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19010_s025", "title": "The payment of wages act, 1936", "chapter": "", "section_number": "25", "section_title": "The payment of wages act, 1936", "text": "Act: The payment of wages act, 1936 (Act 4 of 1936) | India | State | In Force\nSection 25: Display by notice of abstracts of the Act\n\n**25. Display by notice of abstracts of the Act.—** The person responsible for the payment of wages to persons[1] [employed in a factory or an industrial or other establishment] shall cause to be[2] [displayed in such factory or industrial or other establishment] a notice containing such abstracts of this Act and of the rules made thereunder in English and in the language of the majority of the persons employed[3] [in the factory or industrial or other establishment] as may be prescribed.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['labour_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1936.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19010?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19010/act.pdf", "record_id": "500594668a7d0701f3c9", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 307, "original_text_length": 627, "cleaned_text_length": 627, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19026", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19026_s001", "title": "The motor transport workers act, 1961", "chapter": "IX", "section_number": "1", "section_title": "The motor transport workers act, 1961", "text": "Act: The motor transport workers act, 1961 (Act 27 of 1961) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IX: ## MISCELLANEOUS | Section 1: Ins. by Act 4 of 1986, s. 2 and the Schedule (w.e.f. 15-5-1986)\n\n1. Ins. by Act 4 of 1986, s. 2 and the Schedule (w.e.f. 15-5-1986).\n\n( _k_ ) the conditions and limitations subject to which any motor transport worker may be required or allowed to work for more than eight hours in any day or more than forty-eight hours in any week in any case referred to in the second proviso to section 13;\n\n( _l_ ) the form and manner in which notices of period of work shall be displayed and maintained;\n\n( _m_ ) the rates of extra wages in respect of the over-time work done by a motor transport worker in any case referred to in the second proviso to section 13;\n\n( _n_ ) the registers which should be maintained by employers and the returns, whether occasional or periodical, as in the opinion of the State Government may be required for the purposes of this Act; and\n\n( _o_ ) any other mater which has to be, or may be, prescribed.\n\n> 1[( _3_ ) Every rule made by the State Government under this Act, shall be laid, as soon as it is made, before the State Legislature.]\n\n1. Ins. by Act 4 of 1986, s. 2 and the Schedule (w.e.f. 15-5-1986).", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 1, "year": 1961.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/