{"act_id": "IND_state_18999", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18999_s41C_d1", "title": "The factories act, 1948", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "41C", "section_title": "The factories act, 1948", "text": "Act: The factories act, 1948 (Act 63 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: ``` | Section 41C: Specifice responsibility of the occupier in relation to\n\n41C. Specifice responsibility of the occupier in relation to\nhazardoue processes. Every occupier of a factory involving any\nhazardous process shall--\n```\n\n```\n(a) maintain accurate and up-to-date health records or, as\nthe case may be, medical records, of the workers in the\nfactory who are exposed to any chemical, toxic or any\nother harmful substances which are manufactured,\nstored, handled or transported and such records shall\nbe accessible to the workers subject to such conditions\nas may be prescribed;\n```\n\n```\n(b) appoint persons who possess qualifications and\nexperience in handling hazardous substances and are\ncompetent to supervise such handling within the factory\nand to provide at the working place all the necessary\nfacilities for protecting the workers in the manner\nprescribed:\n```\n\n```\nProvided that where any question arises as to the\nqualifications and experience of a person so appointed,\nthe decision of the Chief Inspector shall be final;\n```\n\n```\n(c) provide for medical examination of every worker--\n```\n\n```\n(a) before such worker is assigned to a job involving\nthe handling of, or working with, a hazardous\n```\n\n```\nsubstance, and\n```\n\n```\n(b) while continuing in such job, and after he has\nceased to work in such job, at intervals not\nexceeding twelve months, in such manner as may be\nprescribed.\n```\n\n```", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18999?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18999/act.pdf", "record_id": "81c93a0f98375cee573c", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 375, "original_text_length": 1494, "cleaned_text_length": 1494, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19319", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19319_s050", "title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "chapter": "VI", "section_number": "50", "section_title": "The Waqf Act, 1995", "text": "Act: The Waqf Act, 1995 (Act 43 of 1995) | India | State | In Force\nChapter VI: ## MAINTENANCE OF ACCOUNTS OF[2] [AUQAF] | Section 50: Duties of mutawalli\n\n**50. Duties of mutawalli.—** It shall be the duty of every mutawalli **—**\n\n( _a_ ) to carry out the directions of the Board in accordance with the provisions of this Act or of any rule or order made thereunder;\n\n( _b_ ) to furnish such returns and supply such information or particulars as may from time to time be required by the Board in accordance with the provisions of this Act or of any rule or order made thereunder;\n\n( _c_ ) to allow inspection of[1] [waqf] properties, accounts or records or deeds and documents relating thereto;\n\n( _d_ ) to discharge all public dues; and\n\n( _e_ ) to do any other act which he is lawfully required to do by or under this Act.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1995.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19319?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19319/act.pdf", "record_id": "4c2f8f64317f2da60f6e", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 376, "original_text_length": 826, "cleaned_text_length": 826, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18999", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18999_s41B_p0", "title": "The factories act, 1948", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "41B", "section_title": "The factories act, 1948", "text": "Act: The factories act, 1948 (Act 63 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: ``` | Section 41B: Compulsory disclosure of information by the occupier. (1)\n\n41B. Compulsory disclosure of information by the occupier. (1)\nThe occupier of every factory involving a hazardous process shall\ndisclose in the manner prescribed all information regarding dangers,\nincluding health hazards and the measures to overcome such hazards\narising from the exposure to or handling of the materials or\nsubstances in the manufacture, transportation, storage and other\nprocesses, to the workers employed in the factory, the Chief\nInspector, the local authority within whose jurisdiction the factory\nis situate and the general public in the vicinity.\n```\n\n```", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18999?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18999/act.pdf", "record_id": "5e79cd0d622b2a64626a", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 382, "original_text_length": 743, "cleaned_text_length": 743, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18981", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18981_s018_p0", "title": "The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981", "chapter": "III", "section_number": "18", "section_title": "The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981", "text": "Act: The Air ( Prevention and Control of Pollution) Act, 1981 (Act 14 of 1981) | India | State | In Force\nChapter III: POWERS AND FUNCTIONS OF BOARDS | Section 18: Power to give directions.** —[1] [( _1_ )] In the performance of its functions under this Act—\n\n**18. Power to give directions.** —[1] [( _1_ )] In the performance of its functions under this Act—\n\n( _a_ ) the Central Board shall be bound by such directions in writing as the Central Government may give to it; and\n\n( _b_ ) every State Board shall be bound by such directions in writing as the Central Board or the State Government may give to it:\n\nProvided that where a direction given by the State Government is inconsistent with the direction given by the Central Board, the matter shall be referred to the Central Government for its decision.\n\n> 2[( _2_ ) Where the Central Government is of the opinion that any State Board has defaulted in complying with any directions given by the Central Board under sub-section ( _1_ ) and as a result of such default a grave emergency has arisen and it is necessary or expedient so to do in the public interest, it may, by order, direct the Central Board to perform any of the functions of the State Board in relation to such area, for such period and for such purposes, as may be specified in the order.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['environmental_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "order", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1981.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18981?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18981/act.pdf", "record_id": "11cee9f92dd7f8d072a0", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 385, "original_text_length": 1311, "cleaned_text_length": 1311, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_18982", "chunk_id": "IND_state_18982_s075_d1", "title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "chapter": "IX", "section_number": "75", "section_title": "The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973", "text": "Act: The Andaman and Nicobar Islands Cooperative Socities Regulation 1973 (Act 3 of 1973) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IX: ** | Section 75: Manner of service of notice** :- A notice under the provision to section 62\n\n## **CHAPTER IX**\n\n## **EXECUTION OF AWARDS, DECREES, ORDERS AND DECISIONS**\n\n**75. Manner of service of notice** :- A notice under the provision to section 62\n\nshall indicate the substance of the demand or debt due to the co-operative society and shall be served in the manner laid down for the service of summons in subrule (3) of rule 78. No order under section 62 shall be made until a period of thirty days has expired from the date of service of the notice.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1973.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/18982?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_18982/act.pdf", "record_id": "ccdfd77307fcc1d6def6", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 388, "original_text_length": 686, "cleaned_text_length": 686, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "ma