{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s002_p0", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "XIII", "section_number": "2", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter XIII: ** | Section 2: Sub-S. (1) substituted by S.61, _ibid_ (w.e.f. 14-11-1994). Prior its substitution, sub-S. (1) read as under :-\n\n12. Sub-S. (1) substituted by S.61, _ibid_ (w.e.f. 14-11-1994). Prior its substitution, sub-S. (1) read as under :-\n\n\"(1) A police officer in uniform may require any person driving or attempting to drive a motor vehicle in a public place to provide one or more specimen of breath for breath test there or nearby, if the police officer has any reasonable cause to suspect him of having committed an offence punishable under section 185.\n\nProvided that no requirement for breath test shall be made unless it is made as soon as reasonably practicable after the commission of such offence.\"", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Motor Vehicles Act, 1939"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf", "record_id": "1626fa2fdcbddf2a75a8", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 397, "original_text_length": 805, "cleaned_text_length": 805, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_contro