{"act_id": "IND_state_19025", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19025_s22C", "title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "chapter": "", "section_number": "22C", "section_title": "The mimimum wates act, 1948", "text": "Act: The mimimum wates act, 1948 (Act 11 of 1948) | India | State | In Force\nSection 22C: Offences by companies\n\n22C. Offences by companies.- (1) If the person committing any offence under this Act is a company, every person who at the time the offence was committed, was incharge of, and was responsible to, the company for the conduct of the business of the company as well as the company shall be deemed to be guilty of the offence and shall be liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly: Provided that nothing contained in this sub-section shall render any such person liable to any punishment provided in this Act if he proves that the offence was committed without his knowledge or that he exercised all due diligence to prevent the commission of such offence. (2) Notwithstanding anything contained in sub-section (1), where an offence under this Act has been committed by a company and it is proved that the offence has been committed with the consent or connivance of, or is attributable to any neglect on the part of, any director, manager, secretary or other officer of the company, such director, manager, secretary or other officer of the company shall also be deemed to be guilty of that offence and shall be liable to be proceeded against and punished accordingly.\n\nExplanation.--For the purposes of this section,-(a) \"company\" means any body corporate and includes a firm or other association of individuals, and (b) \"director\" in relation to a firm means a partner in the firm. 22D. Payment of undisbursed amounts due to employees.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "overriding", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": true, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1948.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19025?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19025/act.pdf", "record_id": "72737740fc94ba0646c4", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 422, "original_text_length": 1561, "cleaned_text_length": 1561, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19316", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19316_b000_2_d2", "title": "The Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act 1986", "chapter": "", "section_number": "", "section_title": "The Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act 1986", "text": "Act: The Child Labour (Prohibition and Regulation) Act 1986 (Act 61 of 1986) | India | State | In Force\n(2): Preamble\n\n(2) The period of work on each day shall be so fixed that no period shall exceed three hours and that no child shall work for more than three hours before he has had an interval for rest for at least one hour.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['labour_law']", "has_proviso": true, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": "rules", "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": ["Factories Act, 1948", "Mines Act, 1952", "Merchant Shipping Act, 1958", "Motor Transport Workers Act, 1961", "Plantations Labour Act, 1951", "Children Act, 1938", "Minimum Wages Act, 1948"], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1986.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19316?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19316/act.pdf", "record_id": "4d8f50c37c3b828906ee", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 426, "original_text_length": 328, "cleaned_text_length": 328, "transformations": [], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19318", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19318_s060_5_d1", "title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "chapter": "II", "section_number": "60", "section_title": "The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939", "text": "Act: The Motor Vehicle Act, 1939 (Act 4 of 1939) | India | State | In Force\nChapter II: ** | Section 60(5): Sub-S. (1) substituted by Act 54 of 1994, S. 29 ( w.e.f. 14-11-1994 ). Prior to its substitution, sub-S. (1) read as under\n\n(5) A State Government may prescribe the circumstances under which and the period during which the driver of a vehicle although not engaged in work is required to remain on or near the vehicle may be deemed to be an interval for rest within the meaning of sub-section (1).\n\n_**Corresponding Law.**_ **-** Section 91 corresponds to section 65 of the motor vehicles Act, 1939.\n\n_**Object and Reasons**_ **. -** Clause 91 prohibits the driving of motor vehicles by a person for more than certain hours in a day and the hours of rest the driver should take after certain hours of continuous driving.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "prohibitory", "section_type": "sub_section", "legal_subject": "['general']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1939.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19318?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19318/act.pdf", "record_id": "cee2fdfe8e3f06781509", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 431, "original_text_length": 828, "cleaned_text_length": 827, "transformations": ["normalized_horizontal_whitespace"], "preprocessing_status": "completed"}, "quality_control": {"decision": "quarantined", "audit_flagged": true, "manual_review_status": "not_reviewed", "review_message": "Review status is 'not_reviewed'."}}
{"act_id": "IND_state_19019", "chunk_id": "IND_state_19019_s032", "title": "The inland vessels act, 1917", "chapter": "IV", "section_number": "32", "section_title": "The inland vessels act, 1917", "text": "Act: The inland vessels act, 1917 (Act 1 of 1917) | India | State | In Force\nChapter IV: INVESTIGATIONS INTO CASUALTIES | Section 32: Report of casualties to be made to nearest police-station**\n\n## CHAPTER IV\n\nINVESTIGATIONS INTO CASUALTIES\n\n**32. Report of casualties to be made to nearest police-station** .—Whenever—\n\n( _a_ ) any inland[5] [mechanically propelled vessel] has been wrecked, abandoned or materially damaged, or\n\n( _b_ ) by reason of any casualty happening to, or on. board of, any inland[5] [mechanically propelled vessel], loss of life has ensued,. or\n\n( _c_ ) any inland[5] [mechanically propelled vessel] alas caused loss or material damage to, any other vessel,\n\nthe master of the[ 5] [mechanically propelled vessel] shall forthwith give notice of the wreck, abandonment, damage, casualty, or loss to the officer in charge of the nearest police -station.", "jurisdiction": "state", "state": "andaman-nicobar", "instrument_type": "legislation", "act_status": "in_force", "in_force": true, "doc_type": "legislation", "provision_type": "mandatory", "section_type": "section", "legal_subject": "['property_law']", "has_proviso": false, "has_non_obstante": false, "delegation_type": null, "department": "", "regulatory_body": null, "acts_referenced": [], "defined_terms": [], "amendment_count": 0, "year": 1917.0, "source_url": "https://www.indiacode.nic.in/handle/123456789/19019?view_type=browse", "language_code": "en", "source_publisher": "Legislative Department, Ministry of Law and Justice (India Code)", "mirror_url": "https://oss-data-in.vaquill.ai/legislation/IND_state_19019/act.pdf", "record_id": "c25a465cbadcb48a7999", "preprocessing_info": {"source_record_number": 436, "original_text_length": 876, "cleaned_text_length": 876, "transformations": []